# net-snmp's snmptrapd config. Copy to /etc/snmp/snmptrapd.conf.
#
# By default snmptrapd DROPS every trap unless a matching authCommunity
# (v1/v2c) or matching v3 user is configured -- same "never guess a
# credential" principle as the SNMP poller: add a line per community your
# devices actually send traps with, don't add a permissive catch-all.
#
# "log" writes the trap to snmptrapd's own log; "execute" additionally
# lets exec/traphandle directives below fire for it. We use "log" only --
# the trap gets logged via syslog (see /etc/default/snmptrapd or the
# systemd unit's ExecStart, which adds -Lsd) and rsyslog picks it up from
# there like anything else, flowing into raw.jsonl the same as normal
# syslog does.

# authCommunity log,execute <community>
authCommunity log public

# One line per additional community your devices use:
# authCommunity log another-community-here

# SNMPv3 traps (if any devices send these instead of v1/v2c):
# createUser <username> <authProto> <authPass> <privProto> <privPass>
# authUser log <username>
